ExamAI is a full-stack, AI-powered exam-preparation platform designed to connect students with teacher-
approved learning material. The platform combines retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) chat, teacher-
authored shared quizzes, AI-assisted quiz generation, and student-owned flashcard decks in one web
application. It provides separate workflows for students and teachers while keeping authorization, material
ownership, and academic comparability explicit in the system design.
Students can select a subject, choose the approved materials that should scope a study session, ask
questions, receive answers with teacher and filename attribution, attempt published quizzes, review weak
topics, and generate flashcards. Teachers can upload PDF, PPTX, and DOCX materials, monitor ingestion
status, author or generate quizzes, publish shared assessments, and review class-wide analytics.
The backend uses FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, Alembic, Supabase Postgres and Auth, Gemini, Qdrant Cloud, and
local sentence-transformer embeddings. The frontend uses React, Vite, React Router, Zustand, Tailwind
CSS, and reusable interface primitives. The project demonstrates secure role-based access, metadata-
filtered retrieval, concurrent ingestion protection, structured-output retry handling, server-side quiz
grading, and measured frontend performance. The current implementation contains 82 offiine backend
tests and 63 frontend tests.
The report presents the motivation, objectives, literature and technology overview, project management
approach, requirements, system analysis, testing, system design, results, limitations, future enhancements,
and conclusion of the ExamAI project.